WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.380
- All right everybody
let's close up this hour

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.750
with something truly uplifting.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:04.951
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:04.951 --> 00:00:08.700
(upbeat music)
(audience applauding)

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.550
You may remember just a few weeks ago,

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.300
we had the Oscar winning
cast of the film 'CODA' here,

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.270
it was amazing.

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:15.740
They've helped shine an important light

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:16.780
on the deaf community,

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.690
not just their challenges but
simply their everyday life.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.410
As Deaf History Month continues,

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.380
I wanna introduce you to another
actress bringing attention

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.590
to those who are deaf or hard of hearing.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:28.420
You've seen her in the
movies 'Wonderstruck',

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.450
'A Quiet Place' and 'The Sequel',

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.080
and she signed in the
ASL version of my video

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:33.913
for 'I Dare You'.

00:00:33.913 --> 00:00:35.180
It was really magical.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.970
Now she's just released a
necklace to help encourage people

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.660
to learn American sign language.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.650
Here we go.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.384
Let's say hi to Millie
Simmons and her mama Emily.

00:00:43.384 --> 00:00:45.370
(audience applauding)

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:46.203
Hello.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.450
So it's so great to meet you.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.750
So you lost your hearing
in two months old.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:56.963
But doctors told your mom
not to teach you ASL. Why?

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.630
- That's right.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:02.300
The audiologist told my mom

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.093
that if she learned to ASL,

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:08.030
I would never learn to speak.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:12.080
Though I was very lucky
that she didn't listen.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.580
Went ahead and learned sign language.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:18.240
And also I went to a deaf school.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.150
I grew up going to a deaf school

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.860
and I noticed that some
kids that I was with

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.040
didn't want to go back home,

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.950
and I didn't really understand why.

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:29.440
And then it wasn't until later in life

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:30.949
that I realized they're hearing...

00:01:30.949 --> 00:01:33.710
their parents really didn't learn

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:35.280
how to communicate with them at home.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.210
Only 10% of hearing parents really learn.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.040
And I was shocked to learn that.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.830
So I feel like it's really important

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:46.251
to highlight this issue.

00:01:46.251 --> 00:01:48.560
- Emily, do you wanna tell
us about this necklace?

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:49.470
This is a really cool idea.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:50.820
What does this exactly mean?

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.830
- Yes. The necklace is the sign for mom.

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.890
And so it has the profile.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:57.930
And then the hand if it goes on the chin,

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.030
that is the sign for a mom.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:03.860
And we wanted unlike the 'I love you' sign

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.040
that you see everywhere.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:10.040
We wanted it to kind of
focus and be specific to ASL,

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:14.690
and kind of highlight the
relationship that you can have

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:19.690
when deaf kids have
access to their language.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:20.673
So...

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:21.686
- Everybody

00:02:21.686 --> 00:02:22.519
(audience applauding)

00:02:22.519 --> 00:02:25.060
to pick up the Millie ASL Mama necklace

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.010
and support the Sky High Institute,

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:28.163
go to cutandclarity.co.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.056
Thank you so much Millie and Emily.

00:02:31.056 --> 00:02:31.889
Thank you.

00:02:31.889 --> 00:02:33.240
(audience applauding)

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:34.863
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:34.863 --> 00:02:37.860
(audience applauding)

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.920
All right that's not although
our season long partner

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.480
Pilot Pen Makers of Friction

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:43.580
go to erasable pin of
the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.830
wanna celebrate those creating fearlessly,

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:46.663
just like y'all.

00:02:46.663 --> 00:02:48.240
So they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:49.076
How's that sound.

00:02:49.076 --> 00:02:50.182
(audience applauding)

00:02:50.182 --> 00:02:51.140
(host laughs)

